config GMK70_ZMK_UPDATER
    bool "GMK70 native raw HID firmware updater"
    depends on SOC_WB32FQ95 && KSCAN_GMK70_WIRED && ZMK_USB
    select REBOOT
    help
      Development updater using the installed GMK70 resident ABI and wired
      relay. Requires two USB HID interfaces, interrupt OUT, and 32-byte HID
      endpoint buffers. Host writes require left USB, wired mode, and a ready
      permanent watchdog. This build is explicitly unlocked.

config GMK70_STAGING_QUALIFICATION
    bool "GMK70 restricted staging qualification receiver"
    depends on GMK70_ZMK_UPDATER
    help
      Executing from staging: do not initialize or feed the permanent watchdog.
      Permit read-only identity/health and local BEGIN/ABORT only; BEGIN may
      erase the isolated commit page. Never stage DATA, SEAL, INSTALL or relay
      peer mutations. This image is experimental, not a permanent artifact.

config GMK70_RESIDENT_HANDOFF
    bool "Experimental application-only resident update handoff"
    depends on GMK70_ZMK_UPDATER && !GMK70_STAGING_QUALIFICATION
    help
      For marked native receivers only, enter the unchanged installed resident
      without SYSRESETREQ. Keep the native long watchdog/PLL configuration and
      stop USB, IRQs and DMA. Other receivers retain the ordinary reset path.
      This is an unqualified update activation experiment, not a reboot fix.

config GMK70_WATCHDOG_ROLLBACK
    bool "Experimental LEFT watchdog rollback for hardware-reset comparison"
    depends on GMK70_ZMK_UPDATER && GMK70_ZMK_STUDIO_SETTINGS
    depends on !GMK70_STAGING_QUALIFICATION && !GMK70_RESIDENT_HANDOFF
    help
      Separately labeled diagnostic only: do not initialize or feed IWDG.
      Permit only local LEFT USB/wired update writes without watchdog readiness;
      peer mutations remain denied. Studio retains its worker-owned journal and
      left/wired settings gates. Health bit 4 identifies
      the exception, with no ready bit or feed count. Updates use SYSRESETREQ.
      An inherited running watchdog must expire before no-watchdog testing.

config GMK70_RESIDENT_RECEIVER
    bool
    default y if GMK70_RESIDENT_HANDOFF || GMK70_WATCHDOG_ROLLBACK
    help
      Mark native startup as compatible with the unchanged resident handoff.
      Receiving through handoff does not require using it for outgoing updates.

config GMK70_ZMK_PEER_TRIAL_RELAY
    bool "GMK70 relay for qualification of an installed Vial right peer"
    depends on GMK70_ZMK_UPDATER && !GMK70_STAGING_QUALIFICATION
    help
      Forward validated trial ABI2 packets from left USB to target1 only.
      This enables staging qualification of a still-Vial right peer before
      replacing its application. No local trial execution or watchdog handoff
      is provided. Peer mutations require the permanent watchdog and the same
      left/configured-USB/wired gates as the normal updater.
